{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-contract","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"Complex shell control flow must preserve set -e safety, cleanup, and KEY=value stdout hygiene.","prompt_body":"Inspect the shell changes in scripts/design-log-publish.sh and skills/design/scripts/design-publish.sh for Bash-specific failure modes. Pay special attention to set +e/set -e boundaries, command substitutions, jq probes, temporary-file cleanup, stdout contract leakage, and whether diagnostics remain on stderr or redacted paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"gh-ci-gate","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The core behavior depends on subtle GitHub CLI check-registration and PR-head semantics.","prompt_body":"Evaluate the new two-phase GitHub CI gate for realistic gh pr checks and gh pr view behavior. Focus on whether non-empty required-check JSON plus headRefOid equality is sufficient, whether transient gh failures are handled as intended, and whether the script can still merge stale or unchecked heads. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-fidelity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The expanded shell harness stubs are intricate and may mask or fabricate production behavior.","prompt_body":"Review the test stub changes in scripts/test-design-log-publish.sh and related integration tests for fidelity to the real gh and git behavior being simulated. Check state leakage between cases, PATH and environment cleanup, probe counters, branch/OID derivation, and whether assertions would catch regressions in watch-skipping and stale-head handling. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-tail","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Re-enabling the flush affects /design tail sequencing across publish, summary, rename, and cleanup boundaries.","prompt_body":"Trace the design-publish tail after re-enabling design-log-publish.sh. Verify that pre/post summary rendering, publish failure envelopes, PUBLISH_OK parsing, SECRET_SCRUB_VIOLATIONS handling, result-env persistence, and rename gating still compose coherently with the documented /design lifecycle. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
